<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 53,764 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 53,764 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-01-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 53,764 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Sunday compared to 30,425 tonnes in the same period on Saturday.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>				    Sunday	Jan 25</p>
<p>    Export cargo		18,304	14,120</p>
<p>    Import cargo		35,460	16,305</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, four ships sailed and five berthed. In the next 24 hours, three are expected to sail and 12 are expected to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at Karachi Port:</p>
<p>    Commodity	  Tonnes/TEUs  Ship		   Berthing</p>
<p>Palm oil		 15,000	 Wawasan Megah     29/1</p>
<p>Lubricants	     10,550	 Bakri Orbitor     29/1</p>
<p>Containers		  300	 Ocean Strength    29/1</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
